  "conditions": "a GitHub runner's four CPUs: the load tool on one, the stand-in model on one, the gateway on two, OpenAI's format in and out, the load tool acknowledging every packet at once where an ordinary client waits up to 40 ms. Switched on in Nave: routes by model, falls back, takes OpenAI's and Anthropic's formats, keeps spend by key. No key check, no request log, no limits. Switched on in sub2api: routes by group to upstream accounts, takes OpenAI's format and sends it on as a Responses call, checks the caller's key, counts usage and quota in PostgreSQL. Simple mode, as its docs give for one owner",
